# ^ The official-stockfish/Stockfish commit the prod image runs
# (scripts/engine-assets.sh reads the first line; this comment is ignored). Tag sf_18, 2026-01-31.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-09-06). Until now Stockfish was the ONLY engine in
# railpack.json that was not pinned: `deploy.aptPackages` carried a bare
# "stockfish", so prod's Misty leaf evaluator was whatever Debian happened to
# ship on the last rebuild, while every local bakeoff, replay rig and loss
# audit ran homebrew Stockfish. Live and replay were evaluating with different
# functions, which means no local measurement of a production move was
# faithful. Flagged in the 2026-06-12 klussfix bakeoff verdict as a "separate
# thread" and never closed.
#
# Built from source by the Build engines workflow (scripts/engine-assets.sh)
# and fetched by the image as our own release asset, because sf_18
# publishes no x86-64-sse41-popcnt asset, and this image targets that ISA for
# fairy-stockfish-xiangqi, pikafish-jieqi and pikafish. Do not swap in an avx2
# release binary without first confirming the container's CPU flags.
#
# Bumping this is a behaviour change to the engine, not just an upgrade: the
# leaf evaluator is the largest single term in Obscuro's own ablation table.
# Re-run the strength cell before moving it.
